# Scratch space for generation/heal agents (cookie jars, downloaded
# response bodies, extracted JS bundles) — must live inside the repo
# checkout, not /tmp/: the sandbox's Bash permission allowlist (grep, ls,
# cat, wc, find, head, tail) only applies within the workspace boundary,
# so those same allowed commands still get denied against a /tmp/ path
# even though curl (a network tool, not a filesystem-inspection one) is
# exempt from that boundary and can write there fine. Gitignored so
# nothing here is ever swept into a commit.
.scratch/
